  "description": "Application under Section 73 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 to vary condition 1 of planning permission 24/00703/FULLR3 dated 04/09/2024 to extend the temporary time period for the installation of the sculptures to 20/07/2027.\rCondition Number(s): 1 The sculpture authorised by this permission must be removed by 20 July 2026 and unless\rotherwise approved, the works required for the reinstatement of the land to its condition\rexisting before the development must be carried out by the same date.\rREASON: In accordance with the applicant's request for a limited period consent and to\rensure that the visual amenities of the area are not prejudiced when the sculpture and\rassociated structures are removed in accordance with the following policies of the Local\rPlan: CS10; DM10.4.\r\r2 The development shall not be carried out other than in accordance with the following\rapproved drawings and particulars or as approved under conditions of this planning\rpermission: 'Samuel Ross, Caucus SITC 1:1250 Rev 1', 'Samuel Ross, Caucus -\rPresentation', 'Samuel Ross Caucus 1:100 Rev1'\rREASON: To ensure that the development of this site is in compliance with details and\rparticulars which have been approved by the Local Planning Authority.\r\r\rConditions(s) Removal:\r\rExtension of 14th edition of SITC to allow more time for public engagement - request all existing exhibition remain in place for a further year\rPermission for Samuel Ross's artwork to remain in place until July 2027",
